# Template Conventions

## Placeholders

- Format: `{{PLACEHOLDER_NAME}}` — double curly braces, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
- Current placeholders: `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`, `{{ROOT_FOLDERS}}`, `{{MODULE_NAME}}`.
- All placeholders must be replaceable by `sed` in `activate.sh`. Avoid characters that conflict with sed delimiters (`|`).

## ai_project_index.toml

- Sections: `[meta]`, `[structure]`, `[modules]`, `[entry_points]`, `[commands]`, `[context_loading]`, `[boundaries]`, `[dependencies.policy]`, `[dependencies.external]`, `[testing]`, `[conventions]`, `[conventions.patterns]`, `[conventions.files]`, `[notes]`.
- Use TOML comments (`#`) for examples and guidance — users and AI fill in values.
- `[[component]]` arrays are for inline component definitions; larger projects use separate module files.
- `[context_loading]` maps task types to relevant files (routing table for AI context).
- `[boundaries]` documents architectural invariants AI must not violate.
- `[testing]` describes test framework, conventions, and commands.

## module.toml

- Per-module template with `[meta]`, `[[component]]` arrays, `[dependencies]`, and `[usage]` sections.
- Uses `{{MODULE_NAME}}` and `{{PROJECT_NAME}}` placeholders.
- Target size: 10–40 lines per module file.

## INIT.md

- Step-by-step AI analysis instructions — maintain the numbered step structure.
- Must be self-contained: an AI reading only this file should understand the full workflow.
- References `ai_project_index/ai_project_index.toml` and `ai_project_index/modules/` as output targets.
- Emphasizes context budget awareness: every line costs future tokens.
- Instructs AI to delete INIT.md when analysis is complete.
